t\t\\draw[bmod] (1,0)--(1,0.25)--(.5,.75);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (1.25, 0) -- (1.25, .5)--(1,.75);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{0, 1.25}{east}{\\psi};\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{.5, 1.25}{west}{\\rho};\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{1, .75}{west}{\\rho};\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{0, .75}{east}{\\mathcal{H}};\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{0.5, .75}{east}{\\psi};\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{0.5, .25}{east}{\\mathcal{H}};\n\t\t\t\t\\end{tikzpicture} -\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[anchorbase]\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (0, 0) -- (0, .5) -- (.25, .75)--(0.25,1)--(0.5,1.25)--(0.5,1.5);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (0.5,0) -- (0.5,.5)--(.25,.75);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (.75, 0) -- (.75, .75) -- (.25, 1.25)--(.25,1.5);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (1, 0) -- (1, .75) -- (0.5, 1.25);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{0.5, 1.25}{west}{\\gamma};\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{.25, .75}{east}{\\mu};\n\t\t\t\t\\end{tikzpicture} -\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[anchorbase]\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (0, 0) -- (0, .25) -- (.25, .5)--(0.25,.75)--(0,1)--(0.25,1.25)--(0.25,1.5);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (0.25,0.75) -- (0.75,1.25)--(.75,1.5);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (.5, 0) --(.5,.25)-- (.25, .5) -- (.25, .75);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (.75, 0) -- (.75, .75) -- (0.25, 1.25);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\draw[bmod] (1, 0) -- (1, 1) -- (0.75, 1.25);\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{0.25, 1.25}{east}{\\psi};\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{.25, .5}{east}{\\mu};\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{.25, .75}{east}{\\mathcal{H}};\n\t\t\t\t\t\\btoken{.75, 1.25}{west}{\\rho};\n\t\t\t\t\\end{tikzpicture}","source_id":"arXiv:2609.21644","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"254687fac5377e38cb19ded46f1b4013b726ae32a06d019c3a7cf811423bf1c8","kind":"equation","label":"Equation ten items","ref_key":"fig:ten items","name":"","order":27,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.21644","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1c104b0426ed8403176ae7f8bf7d2426ab6aa302eaf51a632011b062a51bc68b","line":1052,"origin":"latex_env:equation","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:23:46+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":2939,"math_hints":86}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2609.21644","title":"Categorical Lie-Rinehart modules and Shen-Larsson functors","abstract":"We develop a categorical framework for Lie-Rinehart monoids and their weak modules in a symmetric monoidal category. Using crossed homomorphisms, we construct a natural action of the monoidal category of modules over a Lie monoid on the category of weak Lie-Rinehart modules, thereby obtaining categorical versions of the Shen-Larsson functors. We further characterize the conditions under which the category of weak modules admits a monoidal structure and identify the corresponding condition for the associated functors to be strict monoidal. A dual theory for Lie- Rinehart comonoids and weak comodules is developed using cocrossed homomorphisms. Combining the module and comodule constructions, we obtain a bimodule category structure on the category of weak modules. Finally, we specialize the general framework to the symmetric monoidal category of super vector spaces, recovering Lie-Rinehart superalgebras and their associated Shen-Larsson-type constructions.","authors":["Han Dai","Vyacheslav Futorny","Huimin Gao"],"year":"2026","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.21644","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"bbC":"\\mathbb{C}","bbZ":"\\mathbb{Z}","calC":"\\mathcal{C}","ob":"\\mathrm{ob}","id":"\\mathrm{id}","dotlabel":"$\\scriptstyle{#1}$","btoken":"%  \\btoken[vertical spacing]{position}{anchor}{label}\n\t\t\\filldraw[black] (#2) circle (1.5pt) node[anchor=#3] {\\raisebox{#1}{\\dotlabel{#4}}}"},"macros_override":[]},"deps":[],"dependents":[]}